  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1034 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nAdditional frost and freeze headlines are expected again Friday\nnight into early Saturday morning, with a larger part of the\nforecast area likely to see temperatures at or below freezing. A\nhard freeze may occur in some spots as well, especially in the\ncolder valleys of northwest Arkansas. Will forego headlines for\nFriday night at this time to prevent confusion with the current\nfrost/freeze headlines in effect through Friday morning.\n\nAn upper level storm system remains on track to bring rain to much\nof the forecast area from late Saturday night through Sunday\nevening. Drier low level air to the east continues to result in\nsome uncertainty on just how much rain can make it into far\nnortheast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas, so pops will remain\nlower in those places. Temperatures Sunday will remain in the 40s\nin areas that see rain for much of the day.\n\nA warming trend will take place next week, with temperatures\nreturning to near normal levels by the middle of the week. Another\nstorm system may increase rain chances during the latter half of\nnext week, but significant model differences at that time frame\nresults in low confidence in the timing of any precipitation.",
